@* Exercise 032 - MarkupString Rendering (beginner).
   Goal:   Render raw HTML only when explicitly allowed; escape it otherwise.
   Drills: MarkupString, opting out of Blazor's default HTML-encoding.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex032_ *@
@* Rendering `@Rendered` directly would call the framework's AddContent(int, object)
   overload, which always treats a boxed value as escaped text - even a boxed
   MarkupString. Re-checking the runtime type here is what actually lets the
   MarkupString branch render as real HTML. *@
<div id="rich">
    @if (Rendered is MarkupString markup)
    {
        @markup
    }
    else
    {
        @Rendered
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Html { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public bool AllowHtml { get; set; }

